# Local secrets. `.env` carries the ThetaData credentials the option loaders
# read via python-dotenv. It was tracked until now — see .env.example for the
# key names, and set the real values as Codespaces secrets rather than here.
# Note `env/` below matches the directory only; it does not cover this file.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# macOS
.DS_Store

__pycache__/
*.pyc

drift_lab/out/*.parquet
env/

# band_lab/phase1: bulky regenerable logs (summary tables ARE committed)
band_lab/phase1/out/decision_log_*.csv
band_lab/phase1/out/trade_log_*.csv
band_lab/phase1/out/parity_daily_*.csv
band_lab/phase1/out/spec_literal_*.csv

# band_lab/live: runtime state and local secrets — never committed
band_lab/live/state/
band_lab/live/out/
band_lab/live/config.local.toml
band_lab/live/config.local.json

# Session logs from run.py / watchdog.py — they carry balances, share counts
# and fill prices. RUNBOOK_WINDOWS.md §G and RUNBOOK_MACOS.md §G write here.
logs/

# vix_lab: bulky regenerable logs (summary tables ARE committed)
vix_lab/out/trades_*.csv
vix_lab/out/*.txt

# band_lab/v2_dev: V21 writes one row per trade per configuration (~10MB).
# Regenerate with `reparam.py --run`; `--verify` then rebuilds every summary
# number from them. summary.csv IS committed, same split as phase1/out above.
band_lab/v2_dev/out/reparam/trades__*.csv

# band_lab/v2_dev: V23 writes one row per option trade per start date
# (~870 paths x ~90 trades). paths.csv is the summary and IS tracked.
band_lab/v2_dev/out/v23/trades.csv

# V33 sweep output is written live by a long run; committed only when complete
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V33_unhedged.txt
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V35_backspread.txt
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V37_longdated.txt
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V39_openhedge.txt
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V30_straddle_cycles.csv
band_lab/v2_dev/out/V41_strangle.txt

# overnight engine runtime output — never committed
overnight/out/*.db
overnight/out/*.json
overnight/out/*.csv
overnight/out/*.log

# retreat_lab: results a script rewrites on EVERY run. Tracking these made a
# local analysis dirty the tree and abort the next `git pull` — the data files
# beside them (*_daily_ibkr.csv, proposed_ledger.csv, fill_quality_*.csv,
# option_quotes_*.csv) are fetched or measured once and stay tracked, because
# the parity gate and the cost model read them.
retreat_lab/out/tail_screen.csv
retreat_lab/out/dd_levers.csv
retreat_lab/out/xlu_sleeve.csv
retreat_lab/out/scaled_*.csv
retreat_lab/out/hedge_sleeve_*.csv

# The 235-symbol screen universe WAS ignored here, on the reasoning that it is
# "refetchable in 45 minutes and machine-local". That held while the fetch ran
# on the Windows box, which keeps its disk. It inverts once the fetch runs in a
# Codespace: a Codespace is ephemeral, so "machine-local" means "gone when the
# container is deleted", and the 45 minutes is not the real cost -- the IBKR
# pacing budget is. The universe is now TRACKED, ~14MB of plain git objects
# (see .gitattributes: deliberately not LFS, so `.lfsconfig`'s fetchexclude
# cannot leave a fresh clone holding pointer files that die in the CSV parser).
#
# Refetch with `--force` when the bars go stale; the diff is the whole point.
